            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Diane Hawk Mattson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was wonderful. I made it the first time for my daughter's college graduation party and everyone loved it. I liked the fact that I could have the recipe make enough for 60 people and then it gave me exactly what I needed for the ingredients. I did add maraschino cherries for decoration on the top.",
            "datePublished": "2001-05-25T06:13:48.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FIREBOTT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an awesome recipe any time of year. There has never been leftovers when I make it. It is easy and delicious. I always add pecans to mine and refrigerate it overnight. That seems to allow the mixture to settle in a bit. Enjoy.",
            "datePublished": "2005-01-03T18:58:51.903Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lainie44"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used coconut instead of marshmallows, and it was just the perfect sweetness. I used a 1/2 can of mandarin oranges rinsed and drained, walnuts, red and green grapes, and a little amount of the drained pineapple juice to mix the pudding and whipped topping. I would have put maraschino cherries on top but I didn't have any. Next time. It's chilling in the frig right now. It's a modified Watergate Salad. TO DIE FOR! Oh, and I used sliced pineapples, cut up.",
            "datePublished": "2024-08-10T19:12:48.199Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Janice"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wish I had read the reviews before I made this recipe the first time. The best way to say it is that it was very dry. I added a little vanilla yogurt to make it creamier. I did make it again and did NOT drain the pineapple and it was so much better.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-07T06:29:10.880Z"
          },
          {
